      "summary": "Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has stated that organizing elections while the country is at war would be destructive to Ukraine, using the metaphor of a \"tsunami\" to describe the impact. He argues that elections conducted during wartime would fracture and divide the nation rather than strengthen it.",
      "takeaway": "Ukraine's leader has closed off the possibility of elections during active warfare, entrenching the current government's authority for the duration of the conflict.",
      "why_it_matters": "Zelensky's rejection of wartime elections signals that Ukraine will remain governed without electoral renewal during the conflict, affecting European allies' diplomatic engagement and the timeline for post-war democratic reconstruction that many Western partners are preparing to support."
